# Both and the two of us in Russian: оба, двое, полтора
subtitle: "Counting people, pairs and halves in Russian: дво́е, о́ба, полтора́, полови́на and не́сколько, and the of-form that follows them."
tags: ["russian","russian numbers","оба","двое","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/number-cases","grammar/counting-nouns"]
thumb: "band \"Two of us, both, one and a half\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Cheaper and better in Russian: дешевле, гораздо лучше","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/139-russian-cheaper.cast"}

## Both and the two of us in Russian: оба, двое, полтора
stress: new
